      "init": {
        "label": "F · Units COMPUTE — and cancel to a RATIO",
        "body": "True dimensional algebra, not labels: divide a length by a time and the result **is** a speed — the `m/s` is derived from the dimensions. Divide meters by meters and the units **cancel to a pure RATIO** — it reads `5:1`, formats naturally as a **percent**, and an FC can't re-label it `$` (**#UNIT!**): a known-dimensionless number isn't money.",
        "color": "blue",
        "width": 330,
        "height": 170
      }
    },
